<h2>Which Welltory alternative fits your routine?</h2>
<p><strong>Cortisol+, StressWatch, Bevel and Athlytic are options to compare for Apple Watch stress tracking.</strong> Cortisol+ presents a weighted wellness score with HRV and sleep context. StressWatch emphasizes stress trends and Watch presentation. Bevel documents a stress timeline alongside other health features. Athlytic describes recovery and exertion tools for training. Choose by the information you will actually use; this documentation review does not establish an accuracy winner.</p>
<ul><li><strong>Understand the inputs behind a daily score:</strong> explore <a href="/how-it-works/">Cortisol+'s published methodology</a> and <a href="/stress/apple-watch/#walkthrough">recorded interface walkthrough</a>.</li><li><strong>Follow stress trends on your wrist:</strong> compare <a href="https://stresswatch.app/">StressWatch's trend views and Watch widgets</a> with the features available in your plan.</li><li><strong>Review a stress timeline:</strong> <a href="https://www.bevel.health/blog/stress-monitor">Bevel explains its heart-rate, HRV and movement-based interpretation</a>, including time spent at different score levels.</li><li><strong>Plan workouts around recovery:</strong> <a href="https://athlyticapp.com/getting-started/">Athlytic documents recovery, exertion and sleep views</a>. Its recovery score and stress view serve different purposes.</li><li><strong>Inspect the recorded data first:</strong> Apple Health is a useful starting point before adding another subscription. Follow our <a href="/hrv/apple-watch/">Apple Watch HRV guide</a>.</li></ul>
<h2>Ask these questions during a trial</h2>
<ol><li>Can I see the underlying readings and when they were recorded?</li><li>Does the app explain missing data and how its baseline is built?</li><li>Can I tell the difference between exercise strain and how I feel mentally?</li><li>Are the features I need included in the price shown to me?</li><li>Can I understand and control data sharing?</li></ol>
<p>Use your own account's current offer to compare prices and renewal periods. We have not reproduced a current paywall for each app and do not present unverified price ranges.</p>
<h2>Which one measures cortisol?</h2>
<p>These wearable stress approaches should not be read as laboratory cortisol measurements. Cortisol+'s number is a model output, and we have not established its clinical accuracy against hormone testing. A branded “cortisol score” does not remove that limitation.</p>
